{
  "title": "iOS: extract view models for RecipeListView and RecipeFormView",
  "description": "1. ramekin-ios/Ramekin/RecipeListView.swift (500 lines): \
:4-26 has 24 stored properties (7 @AppStorage filters, cache store, search \
task); data loading, pagination, stale-query guards, and Core Data cache sync \
are inline methods on the View (loadRecipes, loadMore, syncCachedRecipes, \
applyCachedRecipes — :322-500). Extract a list view model/store owning fetch + \
cache + filter state; RecipeListFilterSupport and RecipeSummaryCacheSupport \
already exist to lean on.\n\
\n\
2. ramekin-ios/Ramekin/RecipeFormView.swift (480 lines): :12-37 holds ~30 \
field/UI states; the View directly performs photo upload (uploadPhotos, temp \
files, PhotosAPI — :441-461), create/update networking (:399-417), and \
tag-parse logic (:332-365). Extract a form view model; \
RecipeFormData/RecipeFormSupport already exist to build on.\n\
\n\
iOS-only by design: web counterparts are tracked in \
p3-web-recipe-form-state-hook and the general web decomposition issues.",
